    "desiredFields": {
      "content_en": "<p><strong>Direct answer:</strong> There is no single kitchen cabinet price that fits every home. A useful quotation starts with measured dimensions and a written scope for the cabinet bodies, doors, worktop, hardware, appliance interfaces and installation. Compare like for like instead of relying on a headline per-foot rate.</p>\n<h2>Measure the cabinet layout first</h2>\n<p>List the lower and upper runs, tall storage, island or wet and dry zones only where they are actually needed. Note the available wall space, doors, windows, plumbing and electrical points. The wider room layout and connected renovation work belong with the <a href=\"/en/services/kitchen\">kitchen renovation service</a>; this article focuses on cabinet cost decisions.</p>\n<h2>Separate body, doors and worktop</h2>\n<p>Ask for the cabinet body construction, board and finish, door finish, worktop material and edge details to be described separately. Melamine, Acrylic and Solid Wood are possible material directions, but the selected sample and written specification must fit the room and confirmed scope. A lower headline rate can describe a different cabinet or worktop specification.</p>\n<h2>Price hardware and accessories by function</h2>\n<p>Drawers, hinges, runners, pull-out baskets, corner fittings and internal organisers should be listed where included. Appliance positions, ventilation, sockets and lighting interfaces also affect what the cabinet installer must coordinate. Decide which features serve daily use before comparing quotations.</p>\n<h2>Allow for the actual site and installation</h2>\n<p>Existing cabinet removal, uneven walls, service points, delivery access, installation and making good can change the work required. Ask who is responsible for each item and what is excluded. For a wider comparison across rooms, use the <a href=\"/en/blog/built-in-cabinet-cost-malaysia\">built-in cabinet cost guide</a>; for plumbing, electrical, waterproofing and the rest of a kitchen renovation, use the <a href=\"/en/blog/kitchen-renovation-quotation-checklist-malaysia\">kitchen renovation quotation checklist</a>.</p>\n<h2>What to send for a useful quotation</h2>\n<p>Share the location, a plan or site photos, approximate dimensions, existing cabinet condition, key appliances, storage needs and a material direction. <a href=\"/en/quote\">Request a free quotation</a> with the scope you know; a final price and schedule depend on site conditions and the written specification. Site measurement is free within 30 km of the company or service point; travel beyond 30 km is chargeable, with the amount confirmed from the location first.</p>",
      "content_zh": "<p><strong>直接答案：</strong>厨房橱柜没有适用于每套房的统一价格。要比较报价，先按实测尺寸和书面范围，分别看柜体、门板、台面、五金、电器衔接及安装；只比较「每尺多少钱」容易漏掉规格和不包含项目。</p>\n<h2>先量清柜体与动线</h2>\n<p>按实际需要列出地柜、吊柜、高柜、中岛，以及干湿区的柜体范围；同时确认墙面、门窗、水电点位和电器位置。整个厨房布局及关联装修范围由<a href=\"/zh/services/kitchen\">厨房装修服务页</a>承接；本文聚焦橱柜费用如何拆分。</p>\n<h2>柜体、门板和台面分开写</h2>\n<p>请在书面报价中分别注明柜体结构、板材与饰面、门板做法、台面材料和收边。Melamine、Acrylic、Solid Wood 可以作为材料比较方向，但最终仍要结合空间、样板和确认的规格选择。不同规格不能只凭一个单价比较。</p>\n<h2>五金和配件按用途列明</h2>\n<p>抽屉、铰链、滑轨、拉篮、转角五金和内部收纳配件，须写清是否包含。电器尺寸、通风、插座与灯光接口也会影响柜体制作和安装衔接；先根据日常使用决定真正需要的配置。</p>\n<h2>把现场与安装范围算进去</h2>\n<p>旧柜拆除、墙面不平、水电点位、搬运通道、安装及收口，都会改变实际工作范围。应逐项确认由谁负责、哪些不包含。跨空间比较可看<a href=\"/zh/blog/built-in-cabinet-cost-malaysia\">定制内嵌柜费用指南</a>；涉及水电、防水和整间厨房工程时，参照<a href=\"/zh/blog/kitchen-renovation-quotation-checklist-malaysia\">厨房装修报价检查清单</a>。</p>\n<h2>咨询前准备什么</h2>\n<p>提供项目地点、平面图或现场照片、主要尺寸、旧柜状况、电器、收纳需求和材料方向，再<a href=\"/zh/quote\">获取免费报价</a>。最终价格和排期需按现场条件及书面规格确认。距离公司或服务点 30 公里以内可免费上门量房；超过 30 公里会收费，金额需先按地点确认。</p>",
      "seo_description_zh": "马来西亚厨房橱柜费用取决于实测尺寸、柜体和门板、台面、五金及现场安装范围。对照书面报价，了解准备免费报价所需资料。"
    },
